Hi everyone,

I have implemented a visualisation method in R for multi-class data called sinaplot <https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/sinaplot/vignettes/SinaPlot.html>.
The main (and only public) function of the package transforms the input data and then uses ggplot to visualise them.

I am trying to write a geom_sinaplot but I'm a bit overwhelmed with the format. So far I have read these guidelines <http://docs.ggplot2.org/dev/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html> which are quite helpful but I'm not sure where to start.
Will I need to write a new stat? Should I use some geom(s) as a template?

Any advice is very welcome!

Bests,
Nikos

